6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this License,
in one of these ways:

    a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
    (including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by the
    Corresponding Source fixed on a durable physical medium
    customarily used for software interchange.

    b) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
    (including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
    written offer, valid for at
    least three years, to give anyone who possesses the object code
    either (1) a copy of the Corresponding Source for all the software
    in the product that is covered by this License, on a durable
    physical medium customarily used for software interchange, for a
    price no more than your reasonable cost of physically performing
    this conveyance of source, or (2) access to copy the
    Corresponding Source from a network server at no charge.

    c) Verify that the user already received a copy of the
    Corresponding Source for this code, or that you have already
    sent this person a copy.

    d) If the work is embodied in a physical product, and the user
    already received a copy of the Corresponding Source, the information
    you are required to give to satisfy subsections (b) and (c) must be
    in writing and must include information on how to access the
    Corresponding Source.

For example, a dialogue between you and a third party might proceed
as follows:

  Q: Does this product incorporate code from your project?
  A: Yes, and under the terms of GPL-3.0. Here is the source.
  Q: I want a copy.
  A: We cannot provide it because we no longer have the copies.
  Q: Then where do I find it?
  A: You may find it here. [valid URL]

But this is not required. Your obligation to provide Corresponding
Source covers your modification of the object code form, and for
distributions under section 6d.

Non-source conveyance of these materials is prohibited under this
License. All conveyances of object code must be preceded by or
accompanied by conveyance of the Corresponding Source. The Corresponding
Source need not be conveyed to those who already have copies.

If a user already received a copy of the Corresponding Source for code
then you need not keep copies; you may instead arrange for your users
to have access or redirection to a network server that you control,
for no charge. You shall arrange that this access includes the software,
and that it remains fully accessible so long as you maintain the server.

You may charge for the physical act of conveying a copy, and you may
at your option offer to replace the object code with the Corresponding
Source in return for the physical medium or its conveyance with the code.

